<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW-INTEG-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW-INTEG-004" ;
  triage:title "atm doctor emits AtmErrorCode::ObservabilityHealthOk/WarningObservabilityHealthDegraded from two independently-owned classifiers, so the machine-readable code cannot disambiguate log-sink health from retained-diagnostics counter health" ;
  triage:description "qa-pr1196-r1 (ruthless-boundary-qa, independently confirmed by quality-mgr, at feature/aw3-health-and-log-query d9ef17ca3): crates/atm-core/src/doctor/health.rs:69-99 observability_finding() classifies the shared logging sink's logging_state (Healthy/Degraded/Unavailable) and pushes AtmErrorCode::ObservabilityHealthOk or WarningObservabilityHealthDegraded into report.findings. Separately, crates/atm-http-runtime/src/doctor_observability.rs:15-49 append_counter_finding() classifies an unrelated fact -- whether the retained-diagnostics jsonl/timeline drop counters are degraded -- and reuses the exact same two AtmErrorCode values. Both run in the same doctor request (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/storage_and_nudge_router.rs: doctor_projection.project(...) triggers the health.rs finding internally, then line 567 calls append_counter_finding(&mut report.findings, diagnostic_counters) directly after), so a single doctor --json response can carry two findings with the identical code for two different underlying conditions. A doctor --json consumer or alerting rule keyed on ATM_WARNING_OBSERVABILITY_HEALTH_DEGRADED cannot tell whether the log sink is unhealthy or the diagnostic queue is dropping events. quality-mgr independently confirmed both call sites and the shared-code reuse by direct source read. Not a functional bug (the WARN line and remediation text are each individually correct) -- a doctor API-contract/ownership violation: two independently-owned decisions collapsed onto one shared machine-readable code with no single owner, matching the repo's 'every important decision has exactly one owner' boundary guideline. Fix: mint distinct AtmErrorCode variants for the retained-diagnostics counter finding (e.g. RetainedDiagnosticsHealthOk / WarningRetainedDiagnosticsDegraded) and wire append_counter_finding to use them instead of borrowing the logging-sink codes." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "integration_review" ;
  triage:category "arch-gate" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T08:55:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AW-INTEGRATION-REVIEW ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-05T08:50:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AW-INTEG-004/INTEG-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AW-INTEG-004/PR1198-1> ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-05T09:35:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

# CLOSURE (qa-pr1198-r1, quality-mgr): PR #1198 at 8777d9c84 mints two new
# AtmErrorCode variants scoped exclusively to retained-diagnostics counter
# health -- RetainedDiagnosticsHealthOk ("ATM_RETAINED_DIAGNOSTICS_HEALTH_OK")
# and WarningRetainedDiagnosticsDegraded
# ("ATM_WARNING_RETAINED_DIAGNOSTICS_DEGRADED") -- in
# crates/atm-error/src/error_codes.rs (enum variant, as_str, and
# parse_observability_or_warning_code wired symmetrically), with a new
# round-trip test retained_diagnostics_codes_keep_distinct_stable_wire_spellings
# (crates/atm-error/src/lib.rs). doctor_observability.rs::append_counter_finding
# now emits these new codes instead of ObservabilityHealthOk /
# WarningObservabilityHealthDegraded; quality-mgr independently confirmed
# atm-core/src/doctor/health.rs::observability_finding (the original owner of
# those two codes for the unrelated logging_state decision) is untouched by
# this PR (empty diff), and grepped doctor_observability.rs post-fix to
# confirm zero remaining references to the shared codes -- the collision is
# fully eliminated, not just aliased. New unit test
# retained_diagnostics_finding_uses_its_own_error_codes
# (doctor_observability.rs) and an added assertion in
# storage_and_nudge_router.rs's doctor_observability_fields_match_health_projection
# test both assert the new codes end-to-end through the real dispatch path.
# quality-mgr ran `cargo test -p atm-error retained_diagnostics` (1 passed)
# and `cargo test -p atm-http-runtime doctor_observability`/
# `retained_diagnostics_finding_uses_its_own` (3 passed, 0 failed) directly.
# No crates/atm-daemon/ (legacy synchronous daemon) files touched. This
# closes the machine-readable-code ownership collision this finding was
# filed for. This was the last open finding in .triage/phase-aw/findings/.

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AW-INTEG-004/INTEG-1>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/doctor_observability.rs" ;
  triage:line 27 ;
  triage:snippet "append_counter_finding reuses AtmErrorCode::ObservabilityHealthOk / WarningObservabilityHealthDegraded, already owned by atm-core/src/doctor/health.rs::observability_finding for an unrelated logging_state decision" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:branch "feature/aw3-health-and-log-query" ;
